WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.368
-Fred, we just went through,

00:00:02.368 --> 00:00:03.736
you and I, 19 months apart.

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.471
And it used to be that I would
see you all the time.

00:00:05.471 --> 00:00:06.872
And pretty much every day,

00:00:06.872 --> 00:00:08.875
I would know what you were
doing, even the boring stuff,

00:00:08.875 --> 00:00:11.310
and I got to be honest,
Fred, I missed that.

00:00:11.310 --> 00:00:15.981
And I'm also aware that you have
a photographic memory

00:00:15.981 --> 00:00:19.218
and an incredible ability to
remember the mundane details

00:00:19.218 --> 00:00:20.687
of every day of your life.

00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:23.456
-Yeah, I do.

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:25.792
-So to make up for lost time,
I thought it'd be fun if

00:00:25.792 --> 00:00:27.393
I would just pick a random day

00:00:27.393 --> 00:00:29.462
from the last year and a half
and you would tell me

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.966
what you did on
Thursday, May 7, 2020.

00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:35.801
-Oh, Thursday, May 7, 2020.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:39.505
So that would be --
That was a Tuesday.

00:00:39.505 --> 00:00:41.841
May 7th was a Tuesday,
not a Thursday.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.077
-Okay.

00:00:44.077 --> 00:00:49.815
-And that was
my...doctor's birthday.

00:00:49.815 --> 00:00:53.586
So I remember
I had just seen him.

00:00:53.586 --> 00:00:55.387
I had an appointment
like the week before.

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:56.689
And then I was like,
"Oh, it's his birthday."

00:00:56.689 --> 00:00:59.458
So I made another appointment,
you know, just to, like,

00:00:59.458 --> 00:01:01.027
surprise him and say like,
"Happy birthday."

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.395
So --

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.397
-So, when you call him to make
the second appointment,

00:01:04.397 --> 00:01:07.032
do you have to say that
something is wrong?

00:01:07.032 --> 00:01:08.635
Because, obviously,
you just had a check-up,

00:01:08.635 --> 00:01:10.203
so there's not really
a reason to go back.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:14.207
-Yeah, so, I say like,
"I got to see you."

00:01:14.207 --> 00:01:15.942
And, so, I was
like, "I got to see you."

00:01:15.942 --> 00:01:17.176
And then I go.

00:01:17.176 --> 00:01:18.578
And, so, then I was like,
"I'm gonna get a cake."

00:01:18.578 --> 00:01:20.880
So I bought a cake that day.

00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:23.183
This was like 10:15 a.m.

00:01:23.183 --> 00:01:24.184
-Is when you bought the cake?
-Yeah.

00:01:24.184 --> 00:01:25.351
-Okay.

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:28.821
-So, I got a strawberry cake,
only icing.

00:01:28.821 --> 00:01:34.293
-So, what does a cake that's
only icing even look like?

00:01:34.293 --> 00:01:35.862
-Seth...

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:39.799
You know,
it's, like, layers of icing.

00:01:39.799 --> 00:01:41.334
-Okay.

00:01:41.334 --> 00:01:43.669
-So, I go in.
I've got a $100 bill.

00:01:43.669 --> 00:01:45.805
-Wait. Is a $100 bill
to give the doctor

00:01:45.805 --> 00:01:47.206
or to pay for the cake?

00:01:47.206 --> 00:01:49.642
-No, no, it's to give the doctor
as like a "happy birthday."

00:01:49.642 --> 00:01:51.411
I go in, and he's --
-Put it in a card?

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.145
-Put it in a card.
-What did the card say?

00:01:53.145 --> 00:01:57.350
-It said, "Hey...

00:01:57.350 --> 00:01:58.585
I have a photographic memory,

00:01:58.585 --> 00:02:01.754
so I remembered
that it's your birthday.

00:02:01.754 --> 00:02:03.857
So here's 100 bucks.
Do whatever you want with it."

00:02:03.857 --> 00:02:05.592
-That's said that
on the front of the card?

00:02:05.592 --> 00:02:06.626
-I wrote it on
the front of the card.

00:02:06.626 --> 00:02:07.827
-Okay, gotcha.

00:02:07.827 --> 00:02:09.328
-So, I go in,
and he's like, "What's wrong?"

00:02:09.328 --> 00:02:12.898
And I'm like...

00:02:12.898 --> 00:02:16.302
I was like, "What's wrong is,
it's your birthday."

00:02:17.703 --> 00:02:18.904
So, I gave him the cake,

00:02:18.904 --> 00:02:20.807
and he's like,
"You know, you can't do this.

00:02:20.807 --> 00:02:22.242
I have, like, patients.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:25.311
There's, like -- There are
medical emergencies out there."

00:02:25.311 --> 00:02:28.715
I was like, "I know.
I'm leaving.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.183
Happy birthday."

00:02:30.183 --> 00:02:31.650
-Oh, man, so it didn't end well.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:33.419
-Oh, no, no. He smiled.
-Okay.

00:02:33.419 --> 00:02:35.087
-Because -- Oh,
yeah, he wasn't admonishing.

00:02:35.087 --> 00:02:36.322
He wasn't like this.

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:37.590
He was more like...

00:02:37.590 --> 00:02:39.392
You know?

00:02:39.392 --> 00:02:42.095
So, I just, like, waved "hi"
to everyone in the waiting room

00:02:42.095 --> 00:02:43.429
and I just left.

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:45.932
-So, these are people with
serious medical illnesses.

00:02:45.932 --> 00:02:47.666
You walk out
and you sort of wave to them?

00:02:47.666 --> 00:02:49.435
-Yeah, yeah.
-Okay.

00:02:49.435 --> 00:02:52.438
-But I couldn't see their
expression because of the masks.

00:02:52.438 --> 00:02:54.707
-So there's a chance they
were really happy to see you.

00:02:54.707 --> 00:02:57.109
-Yeah, I'm assuming
that they were really happy.

00:02:57.109 --> 00:02:59.411
So, then I went and got
a couple of sandwiches

00:02:59.411 --> 00:03:00.646
at this Italian place.

00:03:00.646 --> 00:03:02.348
-Okay, why two?
-For dinner.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:05.083
So I got a lunch one
and a dinner one.

00:03:05.083 --> 00:03:06.418
-Do you often do that?

00:03:06.418 --> 00:03:08.721
Do you often get your lunch and
dinner at the same time?

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:09.756
-Yes.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:11.691
-Okay.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:17.263
-So, then I had them both
and then drove home,

00:03:17.263 --> 00:03:20.166
parked my car,
watched some cartoons.

00:03:20.166 --> 00:03:21.534
-Oh, interesting.

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:23.970
-To fall asleep before what
would have been my dinner.

00:03:23.970 --> 00:03:25.004
-Okay.

00:03:25.004 --> 00:03:27.940
-So I did a quick nap,
maybe two hours.

00:03:27.940 --> 00:03:29.108
-Uh-huh.

00:03:29.108 --> 00:03:32.077
-And just sort of got up,
and then it was bedtime,

00:03:32.077 --> 00:03:33.212
so I was like, "Okay,
well, that's my whole day."

00:03:33.212 --> 00:03:34.446
-Wow.

00:03:34.446 --> 00:03:37.316
-And I skipped dinner,
and that was -- Yeah --

00:03:37.316 --> 00:03:38.751
-That's amazing.
-Yeah.

00:03:38.751 --> 00:03:39.986
-Thank you so much for that,
Fred.

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:45.158
-Blue shirt, white pants,
baseball hat,

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.226
and then,
at the end of the day, shorts.

00:03:47.226 --> 00:03:48.261
-Wow.

00:03:48.261 --> 00:03:49.329
-Yeah.

00:03:49.329 --> 00:03:50.362
-Over the white pants
or instead of?

00:03:50.362 --> 00:03:52.765
-Over the white pants.

